values ('ap_calculus_ab', 1, '1.2', array['1.2', '1.3', '1.4']::text[], 'vocabulary', 'Limit of f(x) as x approaches c', 'The limit of f(x) as x approaches c is a real number R if f(x) can be made arbitrarily close to R by taking x sufficiently close to c (but not equal to c).', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'The limit depends on values of f near c, not at c. The epsilon-delta definition is not assessed.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-calculus-ab-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_calculus_ab-u1-r1-003; ced=LIM-1.A.1 f(x) can be made arbitrarily close to R by taking x sufficiently close to c (but not equal to c)')
