values ('ap_calculus_ab', 1, '1.3', array['1.3', '1.5']::text[], 'vocabulary', 'One-sided limit', 'A one-sided limit is the value f(x) approaches as x approaches c from only the left (x→c⁻) or only the right (x→c⁺); if the left and right limits are not equal, the two-sided limit does not exist.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-calculus-ab-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_calculus_ab-u1-r2-001; ced=LIM-1.C.1 "The concept of a limit includes one sided limits"; LIM-1.C.4 "if the limit from the left does not equal the limit from the right"; LIM-1.D.1 "One-sided limits can be determined analytically')
