values ('ap_calculus_ab', 1, '1.3', array['1.3', '1.14']::text[], 'list_sequence', 'Ways a limit might not exist', 'A limit might not exist at a value of x if the function is unbounded, oscillates near that value, or has unequal left and right limits.', '[{"label": "Unbounded", "meaning": "The function grows without bound near c, e.g. lim 1/x² as x→0 is ∞ (and lim 1/x does not exist)."}, {"label": "Oscillating", "meaning": "The function oscillates near c, e.g. lim sin(1/x) as x→0 does not exist."}, {"label": "Left ≠ right", "meaning": "The limit from the left does not equal the limit from the right, e.g. lim |x|/x as x→0 does not exist."}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-calculus-ab-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_calculus_ab-u1-r1-007; ced=LIM-1.C.4 if the function is unbounded, if the function is oscillating near this value, or if the limit from the left does not equal the limit from the right')
