values ('ap_calculus_ab', 1, '1.10', array['1.10', '1.13', '1.14']::text[], 'list_sequence', 'Types of discontinuities', 'The CED names three types of discontinuity: removable, jump, and discontinuities due to vertical asymptotes.', '[{"label": "Removable discontinuity", "meaning": "The limit exists at the discontinuity, so the discontinuity can be removed by defining or redefining the function value there to equal the limit."}, {"label": "Jump discontinuity", "meaning": "The limit from the left does not equal the limit from the right, so the two-sided limit does not exist."}, {"label": "Discontinuity due to a vertical asymptote", "meaning": "The function is unbounded near the point (an infinite limit), so the limit does not exist as a real number."}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-calculus-ab-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_calculus_ab-u1-r2-003; ced=LIM-2.A.1 "Types of discontinuities include removable discontinuities, jump discontinuities, and discontinuities due to vertical asymptotes"')
