values ('ap_calculus_ab', 1, '1.12', array['1.12']::text[], 'list_sequence', 'Function types continuous on their domains', 'These function types are continuous at all points in their domains.', '[{"label": "Polynomial", "meaning": "Continuous on all points in its domain."}, {"label": "Rational", "meaning": "Continuous on all points in its domain."}, {"label": "Power", "meaning": "Continuous on all points in its domain."}, {"label": "Exponential", "meaning": "Continuous on all points in its domain."}, {"label": "Logarithmic", "meaning": "Continuous on all points in its domain."}, {"label": "Trigonometric", "meaning": "Continuous on all points in its domain."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Continuity is guaranteed only on the domain; for example, a rational function is not continuous where its denominator is zero.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-calculus-ab-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_calculus_ab-u1-r2-005; ced=LIM-2.B.2 "Polynomial, rational, power, exponential, logarithmic, and trigonometric functions are continuous on all points in their domains"')
