values ('ap_calculus_ab', 1, '1.16', array['1.16']::text[], 'vocabulary', 'Intermediate Value Theorem (IVT)', 'If f is continuous on the closed interval [a, b] and d is a number between f(a) and f(b), then there is at least one number c between a and b such that f(c) = d.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'IVT is not the Mean Value Theorem. It guarantees an input c where f(c) = d, not a point where the derivative equals an average rate.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-calculus-ab-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_calculus_ab-u1-r1-023; ced=FUN-1.A.1 If f is a continuous function on the closed interval [a, b] and d is a number between f(a) and f(b)')
